SUMMARY:Panigiri of Panagia (nine-day)\, Arki
LOCATION:Arki\, Arki\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Arki\, with its 40-odd inhabitants\, has one feast a year worth crossing for: the ninth day of the Dormition on 23 August\, when boats from Patmos and Lipsi bring people for the vespers at the Panagia church and a feast of fish and goat by the sea\, with music and dancing by the harbour. Get there and back on a caique from Patmos or Lipsi the same day\, or stay in one of the few rooms.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/arki/#arki-panigiri-of-panagia-nine-day-arki
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/arki/#arki-panigiri-of-panagia-nine-day-arki
END:VEVENT
